privateData.editorialMd:
Build windowSums

A window is a group of numbers next to each other. Take each window of exactly `k` numbers in `readings`, moving one place right each time. Record each window sum from left to right. If the whole input has fewer than `k` numbers, `windowSums` is empty.

Return the answer

Find the smallest number in `windowSums`. Store it in `smallest`. Complete `fixedPanelsFloorTicket` so it returns `smallest`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `windowSums` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

